  "description": "Erection of a ground floor wrap-around rear extension and a rear roof terrace at second floor level.",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Kentish Town South",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:11:29.241Z",
  "street_name": "Grafton Crescent",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed creation of a roof terrace, by reason of its use, location, size, and proximity to neighbouring properties would result in undue harm to the amenity of the adjoining occupiers due to excessive overlooking resulting in loss of privacy, contrary to policies A1 (Managing the impact of development) and D1 (Design) of the Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed erection of the rear wrap-around extension by reason of its footprint, scale and massing in relation to the host building, would fail to appear subordinate, and be out of character with neighbouring properties along the terrace and surrounding area. As such, the proposed extension would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the property or those adjacent which have been collectively identified on the Council's local list as non-designated heritage assets. This would be contrary to Policies D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the Camden Local Plan and Policy D3 (Design) of the Kentish Town Neighbourhood Plan 2016.\r\n"
  ],
